 "description": "A juvenile Belatz: 2 body regions (B2), a head, 2 eyes, a 2-leaf crest, 2 legs, 2 flaps, a tail; feathers; upright, neck head. It is the type of its kind, a big bird: wings and a beak; big birds of open sky. Coat: colour cobalt; fluff between; sheen between; feathers between; fur reach body only; second colour butter. Face: head between; beak between; crest between; crown tall; eyes small, close. Shape: waist thick; back line level; hind body between; body egg; build between. Legs & tail: tail curl straight; tail between. Proportions: a large body, the head carried high, small eyes, a tall crest, long legs, broad feet, a thick waist, wide flaps.",
